# esp32-c5-devkitc-1-n8r8 -- the first RISC-V target with hardware ON ORDER (P173).
#
# COPIED FROM esp32-c6-devkitc-1 AND NOT YET DIFFERENTIATED.  The C5 and C6 are both RV32IMC
# Espressif parts, so the ship-list starts identical -- but the two boards are NOT the same target
# and this file must diverge once a board is in hand:
#   * PSRAM.  The C5-N8R8 has 8 MB; the C6 has NONE.  Anything gated on heap size (the bignum and
#     rational libraries, larger staged .scm sets) can be far more generous here, and the C6's
#     choices were made for a 4 MB no-PSRAM part.
#   * RADIO.  The C5 is dual-band Wi-Fi 6 + BLE + 802.15.4; this env sets LL_WIFI=1 where the C6
#     env does not.  Anything WiFi-dependent in the ship-list applies HERE and not there.
#   * PIN MAP.  Inherited below as the no-hardware stub, same as the C6 -- see the note.
#
# THIS SHIP-LIST HAS NEVER BEEN BOOTED, on this board or any other RISC-V part.
#
# THIS SHIP-LIST HAS NEVER BEEN BOOTED.  No ESP32-C6 board exists on this host, so the env was
# added to get the RV32 NCG backend COMPILED AND LINKED by a real riscv32 toolchain -- nothing
# here has been observed running.  Treat every line as a starting point, not as a measurement.
#
# Two things in particular a future session must fix rather than trust:
#   * PIN MAP: `boards/pins/linux.scm` is staged as Pins.scm.  That is the no-hardware STUB, and
#     it is used because setup.scm loads Pins.scm unconditionally -- NOT because it describes a
#     C6 devkit.  Writing a plausible-looking C6 pin map without a board in hand would be
#     inventing hardware facts, which is worse than an obviously empty stub.
#   * FILESYSTEM SIZE: partitions_4M.csv, inherited from flash_mb=4.  The C6 devkit has no PSRAM
#     and ~512 KB of SRAM, so the WROVER's sectioned-test problem (the suite does not fit the FS
#     at once) very likely applies here too -- see w3_ai_scripts/wrover_sectioned_tests.sh.
#
# The module list mirrors the S3/WROVER core set because setup.scm loads most of these
# UNCONDITIONALLY (ESP32.scm, WiFi.scm, WS2812.scm, LightSensor.scm ...): omitting one does not
# make it optional, it makes the load fail.  The C6 env does not compile the I2C/SPI/WS2812
# feature flags, so those modules may error at runtime on a real board -- that is a Phase-0-and-
# after question, and it is written here rather than silently pruned so the next reader sees it.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/linux.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/array.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
rxrs/rxrs_syntax.scm

# Serial file+command tunnel: resident LLIP receiver -- needed AT BOOT to accept pushed files,
# which is how the ll_tests suite reaches an embedded FS at all (w3_ai_scripts/llip_test_runner.py).
features/llip-serial.scm

tools/test-framework.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite -- the same lean embedded pattern as the S3 manifests: bench + the NCG fusion probe
# ride the FS image; the correctness tiers are pushed incrementally over LLIP.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm     -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm       -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
